> hi I was wondering if anyone here has some tips for compiling and
> installing Nethack in Linux.
> 
> I have got as far as using make but I get an error message:
> 
> -ltermlib
> /usr/bin/ld: cannot find -ltermlib
> collect2: ld returned 1 exit status
> make[1]: *** [Sysunix] Error 1
> make[1]: Leaving directory `/home/scottm/nethack-3.4.3/src'
> make: *** [nethack] Error 2
> 
> has anyone seen this problem before? I assume I am just missing the
> file termlib but I havent found it on Google yet...

You don't want termlib for Linux, you want ncurses. In the Makefile in
~/nethack-3.4.3/src, comment out WINTTYLIB = -ltermcap and uncomment 
WINTTYLIB = -lncurses. That should do it. Oh, and if you don't have
*that* you should indeed get it from somewhere.

(If I were the Dev Team, *I* would do it; I think most people compiling
NetHack on Unixy systems these days are Linux users. But they probably
have their own considerations.)

